ents, a residue-pair is a unique pair of crosslinked residues, irrespective of the peptides identified (A level of consolidation higher than unique peptide but lower than PPI).^(([0-9]+).(a|b))$This term indicates that a given  protein modification is a derivative of a cleavable crosslinker.The single letter code in Unimod that identifies a specific derivative of a modification. For example, in UNIMOD:1842 (http://www.unimod.org/modifications_view.php?editid1=1842) the letter ‘W’ represents the derivative ‘water quenched monolink’.large-scale study of proteins and proteomes.large-scale study of proteins and proteomes via the use of affinity reagents.large-scale study of proteins and proteomes via the use of mass spectrometers to measure the masses and abundances of charged proteins or protein fragments.study of proteins via the use of mass spectrometers to measure the masses and abundances of charged intact proteins.study of proteins via the use of mass spectrometers to measure the masses and abundances of charged intact folded proteins.study of proteins via the use of mass spectrometers to measure the masses and abundances of charged intact denatured proteins.study of proteins via the use of mass spectrometers to measure the masses and abundances of large protein fragments after partial digestion of denatured proteins.study of proteins via the use of mass spectrometers to measure the masses and abundances of peptides after complete digestion of denatured proteins.Thermo Scientific Orbitrap Ascend mass spectrometer with Tribrid architecture consisting of quadrupole mass filter, linear ion trap and Orbitrap mass analyzers.ANN-SoLo (Approximate Nearest Neighbor Spectral Library) is a spectral library search engine for fast and accurate open modification searching. ANN-SoLo uses approximate nearest neighbor indexing to speed up open modification searching by selecting only a limited number of the most relevant library spectra to compare to an unknown query spectrum. This is combined with a cascade search strategy to maximize the number of identified unmodified and modified spectra while strictly controlling the false discovery rate and the shifted dot product score to sensitively match modified spectra to their unmodified counterpart.The rank of this PSM relative to all other PSMs involving this spectrum, when sorting by the XCorr score.A p-value for the XCorr score, calculated using dynamic programming.A modified version of the XCorr score that is made amenable to dynamic programming calculation of p-values by changing a max operation to a sum.The residue-evidence (res-ev) score measures the quality of a match between a peptide and observed spectrum using a method similar to XCorr, but considering all pairs of observed peaks.The rank of this PSM relative to all other PSMs involving this spectrum, when sorting by the res-ev score.The residue-evidence p-value is computed from the residue-evidence score using a dynamic programming procedure.A p-value that is computed by taking the product of the exact p-value and the res-ev p-value and then adjusting for dependencies between them.The rank of this PSM relative to all other PSMs involving this spectrum, when sorting by the combined p-value.A calibrated version of the XCorr score, computed by dividing the XCorr by the 99th percentile of the distribution of all scores for a particular spectrum.The removal of isotope peaks to represent each ion as one data point corresponding to the ion's monoisotopic mass. It is done in conjunction with the charge state deconvolution.The removal of isotope peaks to represent each ion as one data point corresponding to the ion's most abundant isotopic mass. It is done in conjunction with the charge state deconvolution.The removal of isotope peaks to represent each ion as one data point corresponding to the ion's average mass. It is done in conjunction with the charge state deconvolution.The summing of peaks corresponding to the same mass at multiple charge states and presented as singly charged m/z.The voltage applied in the SelexION device to allow certain ions to transmit through to the mass spectrometer.The versioning of a an extension to a specification document that the current file requires to be read correctly. The version should encode the name of the extension, and some ordinal expression of its revision, preferably in semantic versioning notation. Signals that readers that do not know this extension should return an appropriately informative error if they do not think they can or should try to interpret the file.The versioning of an mzIdentML extension document.ChemClipse/OpenChrom file format.Conversion of a file format to Open Chromatography Binary OCB file format.ChemClipse is part of the Eclipse Science project. Primarily developed by Lablicate GmbH.OpenChrom is an Open Source software for data processing and analysis. Based upon Eclipse ChemClipse.Thermo Scientific Orbitrap Astral mass spectrometer contains three mass analyzers: a quadrupole analyzer, an Orbitrap analyzer, and the Astral analyzer.A TOF-like mass analyzer with asymmetric ion mirrors to direct ions into transversal asymmetric oscillations and ion foil shapes and maintains ion packet for transmission and resolution.Waters Corporation Xevo G3 QTof quadrupole time-of-flight mass spectrometer.Waters Corporation RDa time-of-flight mass detector.Waters Corporation waters_connect software for liquid chromatography and mass spectrometry acquisition and processing.Bruker Daltonics' timsTOF Ultra.v?(d+).(d+).(d+)(?:-(S+))?The versioning of the crosslinking mzIdentML extension document.Bioconductor package Spectra for mass spectrometry data representation and processing.Bioconductor package MetaboAnnotation for annotation of untargeted metabolomics data.Bioconductor package CompoundDb for creation, usage and maintenance of public or library-specific annotation databases and spectra libraries.Expanded tabular result format for metabolomics experi